# Copy to backend/.env (`./dev.sh up` does it on first run). Read by
# `python -m smartmirror` (smartmirror/app/settings.py) and by ./dev.sh.
# MONGO_URI is the only thing this repo shares with the Dashboard repo
# (https://github.com/SmartGlassCube/Dashboard), which owns the database
# and infra/mongo/CONTRACT.md. Point this at whatever Mongo that repo's own
# `./dev.sh up` started. Never commit the real .env (it's gitignored).

# Shared with the Dashboard repo. Local (the mongod its ./dev.sh up starts):
MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/ieee?directConnection=true
# MongoDB Atlas -- the mirror reads content, but also writes its heartbeat to
# ieee.mirror_status, so its user needs read on ieee + insert/update on
# ieee.mirror_status (a plain read-only user syncs fine but never shows up
# on the Dashboard's mirror-status page):
# MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://mirror_ro:<password>@<cluster>.<id>.mongodb.net/ieee?retryWrites=true&w=majority

# Assistant LLM: any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (Ollama, OpenRouter, OpenAI, vLLM)
SMARTMIRROR_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
SMARTMIRROR_LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5:0.5b
SMARTMIRROR_LLM_API_KEY=ollama
# Only if you use the Anthropic backend (check scripts/assistant_acceptance_check.py for exact values):
# SMARTMIRROR_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic

# Camera and microphone. Unset = this machine's default ones. A number picks a
# local device by index; an http:// URL uses one on another machine on the LAN,
# served by `uv run python scripts/lan_media_server.py --allow <this-mirror-ip>` (from backend/)
# there (it prints these two lines for you):
# SMARTMIRROR_CAMERA=http://<that-machine-ip>:8081/camera
# SMARTMIRROR_MIC=http://<that-machine-ip>:8081/mic

# Ports. The frontend is told the WebSocket port when the app starts it.
# SMARTMIRROR_WS_PORT=8080
# SMARTMIRROR_FRONTEND_PORT=5173
# Set to 0 to run the backend alone (start the frontend yourself: cd frontend && npm run dev).
# SMARTMIRROR_FRONTEND=1

# Where runtime files go (hand-tracking model, Qdrant store, content cache). Default: backend/.data
# SMARTMIRROR_DATA_DIR=
